Return a corrected second_largest(nums). It must return the largest value strictly less than the maximum. Duplicates of the maximum do not count. second_largest([5,1,5]) is 1. second_largest([3,3,3]) is None. second_largest([1,2]) is 1. End with one python block that contains only the function.

def second_largest(nums):
    a = b = None
    for n in nums:
        if a is None or n > a:
            b = a
            a = n
        elif b is None or n > b:
            b = n
    return b
